WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.840
 It won't be the first time Jerry will be here. Well thank you everyone. Thank

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.080
 you Jerry for the beautiful

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:14.040
 introduction and we truly have been friends for a long long time. I'd like to

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:20.440
 congratulate my fellow inductees, the accomplishments, the hard work, the

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.720
 service to your communities as just for Mark was and it is an honor for me to

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:32.160
 be inducted with you. Congratulations to all of you.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:40.880
 I'd like to thank Debbie and Ann Hanson, number one, for steadfastly working on

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:41.720
 linking the

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.640
 diverse ethnic communities of Cleveland and making the connections to bring us

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.920
 together and for establishing the International Hall of Fame. We owe them a

00:00:51.920 --> 00:01:00.840
 tremendous debt. Thank you so much to both of you. To my husband who is sitting

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.360
 over there, Bob Crawford, come on Bob, stand up.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:12.320
 As most of you know, I'm going to be anywhere with Bob. We both work together

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.240
 on all of our activities and without his support it wouldn't happen.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.280
 To my family and friends who came today to celebrate this great event and who

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.960
 always support me in my efforts, no matter whether you think I'm crazy or not,

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:33.200
 they're always there taking the ideas, moving forward and always listening to

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.840
 me say, "Don't worry, it'll be easier next year."

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:41.840
 Right? To the members of the Cleveland Cultural Gardens and to the members of

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.040
 the Ancient World of Hibernians, thank you so much for your continued support

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:46.840
 and your

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:53.400
 friendship and faith that means so much to me. The Murphy Irish Art Center is

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:59.000
 the Irish dance school I started 40 years ago and I decided on the name Arts

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.640
 because we wanted to promote more than just traditional Irish dancing.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.520
 A lot of what service I've done has come from my parents, as Jerry suggested,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:15.920
 and my grandfather danced when he came here from Ireland and from that point my

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:16.480
 mother

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.200
 wanted one of her children to take Irish dance and I was the one lucky enough

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:27.940
 to get the lessons. I have now been teaching Irish dance for 40 years and have

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.880
 had thousands of students come through our center.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.370
 It's provided much more than just teaching Irish dance, but it's been an

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:42.260
 opportunity to promote Irish culture to them. It's been an ability to develop

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.280
 and grow and make them use their talents to inspire them to do the work.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:50.690
 To do better than they ever thought they could. To even get to the World

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:56.280
 Championships and the Murphy Irish Art Center and our dancers brought a World

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.080
 Championship to Cleveland before the Cavs did.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:17.080
 [applause]

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:22.290
 I'm here to teach Irish dance, primarily at nursing homes and senior citizen

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:27.580
 buildings all across County and I teach the children to give back their talents

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.080
 to respect their older citizens, to learn how important they are.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.930
 After we finish dancing, students are encouraged to go out and individually

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:44.050
 shake their hands and let them touch their costumes and let them say hello. It's

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.930
 such an important part of what we do. It's much, much more than just teaching

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:48.080
 dance.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:53.790
 In addition, we get the opportunity to inspire them to achieve enough that they

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:59.500
 can actually get to the World Championships. We have to qualify, we have to go

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.470
 through an awful lot of effort. Then we get to take hundreds of people to

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:08.080
 Ireland with us as we've done over 40 years and show them our beautiful country.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:13.120
 Many of our students decide then to go to school abroad because they're

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.940
 comfortable with travel and foreign life, but most of all they learn to love

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.080
 Ireland and they frequently go back, which is the goal.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.110
 So we've had a wonderful run for 40 years and hopefully will go on for a lot

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:31.810
 longer, but it isn't a one person act without all the teachers that I have and

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:36.830
 the wonderful support of our parents who really volunteer so many hours to make

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.080
 all of our activities happen.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:43.080
 We wouldn't be successful at all, so thank you to all of you.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:48.990
 And going back to Jerry's story, you know, meeting him in the Irish Garden in

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:55.540
 1961, I used to go to all the cultural garden meetings and I tell people about

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:59.080
 this and I think they believe me but I'm not quite sure.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:04.520
 But I've been going to meetings for over 50 years. As I was a child working in

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:09.480
 that garden, I used to go to the meetings with my mother because she was the

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:14.080
 Irish delegate and we would have meetings in the red room at City Hall.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:26.300
 And I've been with almost every president of the cultural gardens except for

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.420
 the first two. And so going back to St. Grinsky, sitting in the red room in the

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:29.810
 mayor's office with a big cigar out of his mouth and running his meetings

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:31.080
 etched a memory I'll never forget.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:54.400
 And going on through the future to Richard Conish

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.190
 and the cultural gardens that I think is just fantastic. So I appreciate all of

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:04.020
 them coming. We've seen a tremendous growth. We celebrated our 100th

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:08.400
 anniversary in 2016. And the cultural gardens are so unique.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:16.300
 We are symbolic. We are historic. We are an artistic treasure of the city of

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.400
 Cleveland.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.970
 Today Mayor Jackson and our city councilmen who are here tonight and our Cuyahoga

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:29.400
 County officials for continuing to make Cleveland a place that honors diversity

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.400
 and encourages ethnic pride.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:38.060
 That is so important to all of us. Cleveland is a different place because of

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:41.400
 the ethnic groups that are the fabric of our city.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.780
 And when you look at our festivals and our churches, our music, our plays, our

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:52.400
 dance, our civic and cultural organizations and of course the cultural gardens,

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:57.400
 you can see all of that flourishing in a wonderful harmony.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:06.360
 So a whole group of people of Cleveland will come from different ethnic

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:14.540
 backgrounds, have really made Cleveland what it is today. And all of you who

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:15.220
 are here today are tremendous examples of that where you volunteer and you

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:17.400
 inspire the younger generations to do the same.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:22.480
 That's how I learned to volunteer and I'm hoping that that's how the younger

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:27.400
 generations are going to continue all the hard work that we've done.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:33.450
 So I thank you all for doing that. It's so important to model, not just to tell

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:39.540
 someone to do something, but to actually judge yourself and work with them side

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.400
 by side.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:47.590
 It will make so much more of an impact than simply getting directions. So I

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:52.010
 want to ask you to support the cultural gardens. All of us here today belong to

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:52.400
 it.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:58.670
 There's a garden you can join and represent and work for. I encourage you to

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:04.310
 come to One World Day. It's September 16th on Sunday and be part of a glorious

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:09.400
 celebration of all that makes all of our homelands absolutely beautiful.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:17.180
 So thank you very much. All of you with this community of diverse backgrounds

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:23.080
 has brought richness and success and true joy to our city of Cleveland. Thank

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.400
 you very much.

